azgor wrote:
> This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
> freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

Thanks again!

> [1]: Nudist conduct:  Can be obtained by wearing only one of either
> three non-body armor types (gloves, boots, helmet) at any given time.
> Conduct start is triggered by removing any starting armor (other than
> the allowed) before leaving DL 1. --aristotle73

Conducts are supposed to affect the whole game, however, even including
level 1.  There may be subtle abuses possible if the player can still
wear armor even there.

Also, if you're going to make a nudist conduct, you shouldn't take half
measures.  No armor at all.  (Maybe have an "exhibitionist" conduct for
just doing without body-type armor?)

> [2]: remove secret doors from the first few dungeon levels to aviod
> discouraging newbies --scwizard

The sooner they learn about secret doors the better.  Moving them to
deeper levels just delays the frustration (and their eventual trip to
the help files to discover the (s)earch command).

> [3]: Have attacking a water elemental with a towel (or throwing it at
> them) deal major damage --scwizard

Or maybe just created an angry, animated towel-monster?

Anyway, the fact is towels just don't have that much absorption
capacity, and once it's loaded with water it should be useless for
further hits until dried out -- and towels take a long time to dry
unless Measures Are Taken.

> [4]: You should be able to sell your soul in exchange for a wish to
> peaceful demons summoned by sacrificing your own race --scwizard

As another respondent wondered, what is this thing called soul?

Notice that the attached notes of at least one version of the game
contains a hilarious little screed that directly equates a player's
soul with his score.  Thus, a player that does this should simply lose
most (all) of his accumulated points to that point.

Anyway, it is an interesting idea to give demon summoning a purpose,
but it might be a bit too easy of a way to get an early wish.

> [5]: Limit the number of bones files a single character can get to one.
> This will stop DfVers from destroying bones files as they dig down.
> --scwizard

Those DfVers will create more than a few bones themselves during their
reckless plummets to the castle.  The ecology of the bones directory is
thus preserved.

> [6]: Alternate suggestion to the above: Put a cap on the number of
> bones files that a character can get in a certain number of turns. This
> will stop DfVers from destroying bones files as they dig down.
> --scwizard

See my response to [5].

> [7]: Track "petless" conduct.  Must start with pettype:none, and must
> not tame any monster during the game. --PsyMar

Players sometimes get pets without their consent, through the operation
of magic traps.  Still, potentially interesting.

> [8]: The cursed Frost Brand should freeze (as opposed to weld) itself
> to your hand. --Grunt

If the player is warmed, will he be able to release it?  I like adding
additional flavor to the artifacts.

> [9]: the time it takes to forget a spell should be proportional to the
> character's Wisdom. --lament

I disagree, I'm aware of no correlation between a person's being wise
and his long-term memory.

> [10]: Being a male Valkyrie should be a minor trouble, when praying,
> and lead to reversion to female. --SpeedEvil

Heh, clever!

> [11]: If you dip a wraith corpse into a potion of holy water, you you
> get a uncursed potion of gain level --scwizard

Interesting.  Note, however, that potions of gain level are much more
useful than wraith corpses, because of alchemy.  (And because if the
wraith corpse is rotten and that interrupts your meal, you won't get
the level.)

> [12]: Entering an armor store naked has a chance of the shopkeeper
> giving you a free robe. --aristotle73

Hm, I don't think so.  However, maybe he SHOULD bar the door: "No
shirt, no service!"

> [13]: If you get blasted by an item you wish for from a magic lamp, the
> dump should not show the lamp as magic. --SpeedEvil

This sounds like more of a bug than a YANI.  Report it to the devteam.

> [14]: Elven weapons enchant to +9 --jmr

We already covered this one in collection #13.

> [15]: A diving helmet.  Combine with an oilskin cloak to go for a walk
> in the moat. --Grunt

Basically, then, this is a source of "magic" breathing.  That makes the
amulet less useful, which in turn makes the other amulets MORE useful.
Still, it'd be nice to have new item types.

> [16]: Correct the spelling of "Archeologist" to "Archaeologist".
> --aristotle73

That's a variant spelling, not a misspelling.

> [17]: The timeout for levitation granted by a cursed potion goes down
> quicker when floating over water or lava. --ekiM

Why?  Sheer maliciousness?  Bad idea if so.

